              "printed_page": 532,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Metastatic bone tumors (transitional cell,",
              "pdf_page": 614,
              "printed_page": 532,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "The benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy is prostatic, mammary, thyroid, apocrine gland unknown, but it may be considered for anal sac carcinomas). high-grade tumors; consult a veterinary",
              "pdf_page": 614,
              "printed_page": 532,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Tumors that locally invade adjacent bone oncologist for current recommendations. (nasal carcinoma; oral squamous cell",
              "pdf_page": 614,
              "printed_page": 532,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "CONTRAINDICATIONS/POSSIBLE",
